 "observations": [
  "The page number «209» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the right the number of the table, «Tab. 94», in bold sans serif, underlined. At the foot, the signature line of the printed sheet: «D. K. D. Vidensk. Selsk. Skr., 7. Række, hist. og filos. Afd. III. 1.» on the left and the sheet number «27» on the right; recorded here, not transcribed as a line. The page has no title: the folios of the manuscripts stand at the right above the double rule of the first field, in two lines of their own, «C 92r, O 148r,» and «N 58v», the letters raised, the second without its point: see the critical note (L01-L02).",
  "The page holds three fields, as pp. 206-208 (JP2 0238-0240): «Viginti gradus Tauri» (L03), «Viginti quinque gradus Tauri» (L15) and «Triginta gradus Tauri» (L23), the ascendant at 20°, 25° and 30° of Taurus, with the numbers for the sextile, the quadrature and the trine (L04, L16, L24); headings and numbers in bold. The heads of the columns of the first field as on p. 208 (JP2 0240, L05-L08), from Taurus to Libra, with «Horoscopus» in each and without notes (L05-L08); the head of the minutes of Taurus reads «Mln.» (L08; critical note). The second and the third field have no heads. Double rules divide the fields.",
  "The numbers at the head of a field, as on pp. 206-208 (JP2 0238-0240), are a third, a half and two thirds of one number. In the second field it is the last number of the field, 160° 31′ (L22): 53° 30.3′, 80° 15.5′ and 107° 0.7′, printed 53° 30′, 80° 16′ and 107° 0′ (L16), the 107 the editor's for the 57 of all three manuscripts (note f). In the first field the sextile 52° 29′ and the quadrature 78° 44′ (L04) are a third and a half of the last number, 157° 28′ (L14), whose two thirds are 104° 58.7′, where the trine has 104° 9′, the editor's 9 for the 109 of the manuscripts (note b). In the third field the sextile 54° 37′ and the trine 109° 13′ (L24) are a third and two thirds of the last number, 163° 50′ (L30), the 54 the editor's for the 104 of the manuscripts (note g); its half is 81° 55′, where the quadrature has 81° 45′, the 81 the editor's for the 71 of the manuscripts (note h): see the critical note. The same three numbers, with 81° 55′, stand at the head of the field of 15° of Taurus on p. 208 (JP2 0240, L24).",
  "Suter's first example (p. 100, JP2 0132, L30-L37, and p. 101, JP2 0133, L01-L09) uses the second field: the ascendant at 25° of Taurus and the planet at 5° of Gemini give 26° 45′ (L17), and with the sextile 53° 30′ (L16) the sum 80° 15′, which falls between 74° 23′ and 80° 23′ at 20° and 25° of Cancer (L20-L21); the interpolation gives 24° 53.3′ of Cancer for the left sextile, Suter's 24° 53′.",
  "The columns, as on p. 208 (JP2 0240): in Taurus and Gemini the three fields lie above the oblique ascensions from the beginning of Taurus for 38° 30′ (computed with the obliquity 23° 35′), by up to 27′, 34′ and 59′; at the end of Libra they reach 157° 28′, 160° 31′ and 163° 50′, where the oblique ascension from the beginning of Taurus is 198° 42′.",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked by the other fields, which differ by 5° of the ascendant (on p. 208, JP2 0240, those of 5°, 10° and 15° of Taurus), and by the steps of the columns: the edition's readings are the nearer in the quadrature of the first field (note a, L04: the 44 of C and O against N's 84; half of 157° 28′ is 78° 44′), at 15° of Libra in the first (note c, L11: the 147 of O and N against C's 148, the steps 3° 18′ and 3° 17′ against 4° 18′ and 2° 17′), at 10° of Taurus and of Cancer in the second (notes d and e, L18: the 7 of O and N against C's 6, the steps 3° 35′ and 3° 35′ against 2° 35′ and 4° 35′; C's 62 against O's 92), and at 10° and 15° of Cancer, 10° of Leo and 20° of Virgo in the third (notes i, k, l and m, L26-L28: C's 63, 69 and 97 against O's 93, 99 and 93; the 135 of O and N against C's 125). The editor's corrections of the readings common to C, O and N agree with the rule of the heads in notes f, g and h, and with the steps of Libra in the third field in notes n and o (L29-L30: 160 and 163 for 190 and 193; the steps 3° 20′ to 3° 40′); that of note b does not (above).",
  "Without variants: in the first field the column of Leo rises from 85° 28′ at the end of Cancer by 5° 10′, 7° 12′, 4° 43′, 5° 14′, 4° 45′ and 2° 51′ (L09-L14), and by 4° 32′ into Virgo; at 10° to 25° of Leo it stands 12′ to 45′ above the second field (97° 50′, 102° 33′, 107° 47′, 112° 32′ against 97° 5′, 102° 15′, 107° 25′, 112° 20′) and 3° 15′ to 3° 49′ above the field of 15° of Taurus on p. 208 (JP2 0240, L26-L29). In the third field 97° 0′ at 10° of Leo (L26) stands between the steps 4° 25′ and 6° 20′.",
  "The 1 of «15» in the first column of the first field (L11) is bent at its foot; specks between the columns; not transcribed."
